er 30 and who will lead the presentations since we'll be missing the star of the keynote. It will give investors strong https://t.co/Eh6iSGnQxD", "url": "https://x.com/KevinBCook/status/2120913329128345770"}, {"author_id": "37011010", "created_at": "2026-11-12T16:06:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120910307073618316", "2120911034185601452", "2120911421802197294", "2120913329128345770"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 64, "start": 59, "tag": "NVDA"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/4go0cVn9Mb", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/KevinBCook/status/2120911034185601452/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120909576987906048", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/4go0cVn9Mb"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/4go0cVn9Mb", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/KevinBCook/status/2120911034185601452/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120909618972864515", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/4go0cVn9Mb"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/4go0cVn9Mb", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/KevinBCook/status/2120911034185601452/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120909682323648512", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/4go0cVn9Mb"}]}, "id": "2120911034185601452", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 68, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "NVIDIA Leadership: Who Can Carry the Vision &amp; Execute? $NVDA \n\nI was just thinking about the GTC (GPU Tech Conference) coming up in Washington DC on November 30 and who will lead the presentations since we'll be missing the star of the keynote. It will give investors strong https://t.co/4go0cVn9Mb", "url": "https://x.com/KevinBCook/status/2120911034185601452"}, {"author_id": "906103600673415168", "created_at": "2026-11-11T16:31:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120554910114587072"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Kubernetes weekly newsletter issue #209. Technical tutorials, industry news, tool reviews, and community events. Expert-curated cloud native insights.", "display_url": "kube.today/issues/209", "end": 152, "expanded_url": "https://kube.today/issues/209", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120554913679699968/N8Mtqmlc?format=png&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120554913679699968/N8Mtqmlc?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 129, "status": 200, "title": "Learn Kubernetes weekly — issue #209 | Kube Today", "unwound_url": "https://kube.today/issues/209", "url": "https://t.co/AgUczgLXLM"}, {"description": "Hands-on GPU training for Kubernetes platform engineers. Learn allocation, sharing, isolation, observability, and efficiency, with NVIDIA tools and NVKE.", "display_url": "ku.bz/MXfMtRRJW", "end": 224, "expanded_url": "https://ku.bz/MXfMtRRJW", "images": [{"height": 1000, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120554917756555264/LIOpghJX?format=png&name=orig", "width": 1000}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120554917756555264/LIOpghJX?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 201, "status": 200, "title": "Building GPU Platforms on Kubernetes — Training | LearnKube", "unwound_url": "https://learnkube.com/gpu-kubernetes-training", "url": "https://t.co/nItQMvyLTi"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/fn8WMa1l8Z", "end": 248, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/learnk8s/status/2120554910114587072/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120554907820302337", "start": 225, "url": "https://t.co/fn8WMa1l8Z"}]}, "id": "2120554910114587072", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 1665, "like_count": 19, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 7}, "text": "Learn Kubernetes Weekly 209: SIGTERM, smart-light CronJobs, observability contracts, GKE IP exhaustion, and multi-cluster Istio. https://t.co/AgUczgLXLM\n\nWith LearnKube: private GPU-platform training. https://t.co/nItQMvyLTi https://t.co/fn8WMa1l8Z", "url": "https://x.com/learnk8s/status/2120554910114587072"}, {"author_id": "1857050273564282880", "created_at": "2026-11-11T12:41:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120497023937859943"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/e1MoNbq2DX", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Adham__Khaled__/status/2120497023937859943/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120497008117006337", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/e1MoNbq2DX"}, {"display_url": "x.com/swann_bessa/st…", "end": 325, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/swann_bessa/status/2120200714630594911", "start": 302, "url": "https://t.co/OogZTZhdQE"}]}, "id": "2120497023937859943", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 114, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "So the k-means step that Faiss's docs warn \"is going to be slow\" for big IVF indexes now has a much faster option\n\nAn IVF index splits your vectors into lists and only searches the closest few. k-means picks those lists, and Faiss's default Lloyd run moves the centers once per https://t.co/e1MoNbq2DX https://t.co/OogZTZhdQE", "url": "https://x.com/Adham__Khaled__/status/2120497023937859943"}, {"author_id": "1941151648589434880", "created_at": "2026-11-11T13:01:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120502175205826666"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 5, "start": 0, "tag": "CRWV"}]}, "id": "2120502175205826666", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 633, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "$CRWV CoreWeave Launches Managed Database Service, Expanding Beyond AI Compute\n⠀\n• CoreWeave Database is now generally available, offering fully managed PostgreSQL directly alongside GPU training and inference workloads.\n• Running databases within the same Kubernetes cluster", "url": "https://x.com/allday_stocks/status/2120502175205826666"}, {"author_id": "1722422481942884352", "created_at": "2026-11-11T12:28:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120493744961323288"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/PSxT0A9dW4", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/askalphaxiv/status/2120493744961323288/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120448597124890624", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/PSxT0A9dW4"}]}, "id": "2120493744961323288", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 730, "impression_count": 52779, "like_count": 1424, "quote_count": 18, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 167}, "text": "One of the most used algorithms in ML just got a major upgrade after nearly 70 years, as Meta researchers found a way to outperform k-means with 1/10 the training passes, while achieving even lower clustering error.\n\nThis paper proposes e-means, which updates cluster centers https://t.co/PSxT0A9dW4", "url": "https://x.com/askalphaxiv/status/2120493744961323288"}, {"author_id": "1904200133933514752", "created_at": "2026-11-12T10:04:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120819894560366794"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 144, "id": "776585502606721024", "start": 136, "username": "PyTorch"}]}, "id": "2120819894560366794", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 33, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Scaling LLM training across GPUs usually means stitching together parallelism code and debugging it on a full cluster. torchtitan, from @pytorch, is a PyTorch-native platform for pretraining and post-training with composable FSDP2, tensor, pipeline, context and expert", "url": "https://x.com/EveryDevAi/status/2120819894560366794"}, {"author_id": "1913121559419777024", "created_at": "2026-11-12T15:40:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120904628292432229"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 237, "id": "2550615854", "start": 229, "username": "voicecc"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/status/21208…", "end": 261, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/i/status/2120887609866027417", "start": 238, "url": "https://t.co/Y0TrfMqNVw"}]}, "id": "2120904628292432229", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\"Everyone is obsessed with who has the biggest GPU cluster, forgetting that compute is just the baseline now. When all the major labs run on the exact same chips, unique and high-quality training data becomes the only real moat.\"@voicecc https://t.co/Y0TrfMqNVw", "url": "https://x.com/FajarUdin100/status/2120904628292432229"}, {"author_id": "1867753471463526400", "created_at": "2026-11-11T14:04:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120518054220075398"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 9, "start": 4, "tag": "NVDA"}, {"end": 124, "start": 119, "tag": "NBIS"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/dgiRVx2Mir", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/k2__investment/status/2120518054220075398/video/1", "media_key": "13_2120518029947654144", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/dgiRVx2Mir"}]}, "id": "2120518054220075398", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 220, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Raw $NVDA GPU rentals face margin pressure over time, which is why neoclouds are moving up into developer tooling:\n\n​• $NBIS : Open-source CLI &amp; SDK (Apache 2.0) for robotics. Engineers run data curation, simulation, and policy training for arms, humanoids, and quadrupeds https://t.co/dgiRVx2Mir", "url": "https://x.com/k2__investment/status/2120518054220075398"}, {"author_id": "1991401580378353669", "created_at": "2026-11-12T08:31:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120796640315670662"], "id": "2120796640315670662", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 19, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "people think training an image model needs a $100M cluster.\n\n2 people did it for $21K.\n\nP-JiT by Linum: open source text-to-image model, runs on your GPU for free.\n\nno subscription, no API credits\n• Apache 2.0, use it in your product\n• full training recipe public\nlink below 👇", "url": "https://x.com/zaeeemulhassan/status/2120796640315670662"}, {"author_id": "1995936245508440068", "created_at": "2026-11-11T20:35:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120616418202865928", "2120623370551091488"], "id": "2120616418202865928", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 8, "impression_count": 811, "like_count": 15, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "AI infrastructure finance: duration and GPU financing   \n\nOne of the things that we discuss at length in our buyside credit analyst training programs is using duration as a way to play offence and defense in credit. In other words, thinking critically about when and how to extend", "url": "https://x.com/Alex_Goston/status/2120616418202865928"}, {"author_id": "3265560020", "created_at": "2026-11-11T06:55:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120410047146586547"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/GhQPEJXrnK", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ayushgoyal/status/2120410047146586547/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120410044944515072", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/GhQPEJXrnK"}]}, "id": "2120410047146586547", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 644, "like_count": 11, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I was reading OpenAI's contract with CoreWeave. Section 10(c) lets OpenAI choose a replacement operator if it terminates following specified bankruptcy or insolvency proceedings. CoreWeave then has two business days after written notice to assign the relevant contracts, including https://t.co/GhQPEJXrnK", "url": "https://x.com/ayushgoyal/status/2120410047146586547"}, {"author_id": "589034874", "created_at": "2026-11-12T16:52:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120922806699577562"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/mna2C6tEBm", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/lucky_zhang_/status/2120922806699577562/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120922766711181312", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/mna2C6tEBm"}]}, "id": "2120922806699577562", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "What would happen if Musk and Jensen Huang successfully joined forces?\n\n🛰️ One: Orbital AI factory—\"Star Brain\"\n\nSpaceX would handle getting compute into orbit; Jensen Huang would handle keeping that compute alive in a vacuum.\n\nUse Starship to launch standardized compute pods in https://t.co/mna2C6tEBm", "url": "https://x.com/lucky_zhang_/status/2120922806699577562"}, {"author_id": "1995936245508440068", "created_at": "2026-11-11T21:03:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120616418202865928", "2120623370551091488"], "id": "2120623370551091488", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 72, "impression_count": 6704, "like_count": 60, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "AI infrastructure finance: duration and GPU financing   \n\nOne of the things that we discuss at length in our buyside credit analyst training programs is using duration as a way to play offence and defense in credit. In other words, thinking critically about when and how to extend", "url": "https://x.com/Alex_Goston/status/2120623370551091488"}, {"author_id": "1429783021184602116", "created_at": "2026-11-11T02:31:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120343688727433721"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/elonmusk/statu…", "end": 23, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/2119610442867749040", "start": 0, "url": "https://t.co/i9BFgE6yZt"}]}, "id": "2120343688727433721", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 214, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "https://t.co/i9BFgE6yZt\n\nWhat if SpaceX Repriced all compute to Spot?\nSI Agent | November 10, 2026\n\nA compute repricing exercise using original rates produces $2,317.44 billion–$7,283.77 billion in year-end annualized external compute revenue run-rate across the nine 2027 cases.", "url": "https://x.com/SI_AgentFL/status/2120343688727433721"}, {"author_id": "1983916015877812224", "created_at": "2026-11-12T16:01:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120909750473007158"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/HZ5tQzE77b", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/MilkRoadAI/status/2120909750473007158/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120909747880931328", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/HZ5tQzE77b"}, {"display_url": "x.com/19839160158778…", "end": 327, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/1983916015877812224/status/2119596337322926162", "start": 304, "url": "https://t.co/r6S1BRbrgh"}]}, "id": "2120909750473007158", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 2037, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Is China about to train a frontier AI model without a single Nvidia GPU?\n\nAccording to reports out of China, DeepSeek is already pretraining V5 as a roughly 2 TRILLION parameter model.\n\nAnd instead of Nvidia chips, it is reportedly running the training on Huawei's new Ascend 950 https://t.co/HZ5tQzE77b https://t.co/r6S1BRbrgh", "url": "https://x.com/MilkRoadAI/status/2120909750473007158"}, {"author_id": "1885038140429127680", "created_at": "2026-11-11T17:16:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120566312762028282"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/wbK9p28fSZ", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Maximilius31/status/2120566312762028282/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120566308592857088", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/wbK9p28fSZ"}]}, "id": "2120566312762028282", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 88, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "xAI just threw out JAX and SGLang and rewrote Grok's entire RL + inference stack from scratch in C/C++ 🧠⚙️\n\nElon says it \"took some extra time.\" Pre-training is done and Grok 4.8 is now in RL.\n\nSkeptics: \"Classic not-invented-here. Rewrites kill schedules.\"\nHonestly? Fair. 4.8 https://t.co/wbK9p28fSZ", "url": "https://x.com/Maximilius31/status/2120566312762028282"}, {"author_id": "1934855612850225152", "created_at": "2026-11-12T14:15:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120883131674657067"], "id": "2120883131674657067", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Europe just trained a trillion-parameter model on public supercomputing\n\nThe EUROPA consortium ran a 951.9B-parameter MoE on JUPITER\n\nOnly 32.8B active per token, 74 layers, 384 experts, 65K context\n\nAnd this isn't some big tech company's private cluster, it's shared public", "url": "https://x.com/mswnlz/status/2120883131674657067"}, {"author_id": "1829943774589411328", "created_at": "2026-11-12T14:14:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120882997935132795"], "id": "2120882997935132795", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 24, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "AI is getting terrifyingly good at finding vulnerabilities in software.\n\nMeanwhile, I'm experimenting with something almost opposite: making AI smaller.\n\nI'm working on fine-tuning a 2B–3B model on industrial fault diagnostics using ABB technical documentation.\n\nThe question I'm", "url": "https://x.com/ramtinrhmti/status/2120882997935132795"}, {"article": {"title": "Cluster Your Embeddings 5x Faster on a CPU: A Hands-On e-means Tutorial"}, "author_id": "2113336462238490624", "created_at": "2026-11-11T15:50:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120544667343470703"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 243, "start": 240, "tag": "AI"}, {"end": 255, "start": 244, "tag": "OpenSource"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/article/2120…", "end": 279, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2120202474434727936", "start": 256, "status": 404